<!-- rdf_db_network_loader -->
<g id="node1" class="node">
<title>rdf_db_network_loader</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="438.61,-3968 103.5,-3968 103.5,-3788 438.61,-3788 438.61,-3968"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="176.06" y="-3928" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDbNetworkLoader</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="132.06" y="-3900" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Builds or updates an IIDM network from a</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="133.06" y="-3882" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">scenario, in local query mode (bulk fetch,</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="123.56" y="-3864" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">catalogs run locally) or remote (catalogs run</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="222.06" y="-3846" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">on the server).</text>
</g>
<!-- rdf_database_config -->
<g id="node2" class="node">
<title>rdf_database_config</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="454.11,-3100 88,-3100 88,-2920 454.11,-2920 454.11,-3100"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="213.56" y="-3069" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDatabase</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="116.06" y="-3041" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Immutable description of a database: endpoint</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="108.06" y="-3023" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">or the in&#45;process memory backend, query mode,</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="132.06" y="-3005" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">fetch and upload parallelism, gzip, cache.</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="127.56" y="-2987" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Says nothing about which data &#45; that is the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="151.06" y="-2969" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">scenario, an argument of every call.</text>
</g>
<!-- rdf_db_difference_sink -->
<g id="node3" class="node">
<title>rdf_db_difference_sink</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="3449.02,-4211 3077.91,-4211 3077.91,-4031 3449.02,-4031 3449.02,-4211"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3105.97" y="-4180" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDbDifferenceSink / RdfDbExport</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3135.97" y="-4152" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">The DifferenceSink of the database: a</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3097.97" y="-4134" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">recorded change becomes two immutable named</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3114.97" y="-4116" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">graphs and one metadata node, written by a</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3114.47" y="-4098" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">single guarded INSERT ... WHERE that also</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3137.47" y="-4080" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">carries the linear&#45;chain, duplicate and</text>
</g>
<!-- checkpoint -->
<g id="node4" class="node">
<title>checkpoint</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="447.11,-3390 95,-3390 95,-3210 447.11,-3210 447.11,-3390"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="221.56" y="-3359" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">Checkpoint</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="127.06" y="-3331" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Folds the differences of a snapshot into full</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="115.06" y="-3313" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">graphs on the database: COPY per profile, the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="132.56" y="-3295" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">three replace operations per difference, a</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="126.06" y="-3277" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">header rewrite, then pdb:full on the existing</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="129.56" y="-3259" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">snapshot. No new root, so the chain stays</text>
</g>
<!-- rdf_db_provenance -->
<g id="node5" class="node">
<title>rdf_db_provenance</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="1180.72,-4725 827.61,-4725 827.61,-4545 1180.72,-4545 1180.72,-4725"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="923.67" y="-4685" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDbProvenance</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="847.67" y="-4657" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Network extension recording the database, the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="849.17" y="-4639" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">scenario, the graphs and the stored model per</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="876.67" y="-4621" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">profile a network was built from or last</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="875.17" y="-4603" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">updated to. Deliberately not serialised.</text>
</g>
<!-- diff_update_planner -->
<g id="node6" class="node">
<title>diff_update_planner</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="3443.52,-4501 3083.41,-4501 3083.41,-4321 3443.52,-4321 3443.52,-4501"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3182.97" y="-4470" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">DiffUpdatePlanner</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3125.47" y="-4442" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Pure decision over catalogue rows: is the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3122.47" y="-4424" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">network already there, is it on the chain of</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3123.97" y="-4406" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">the target and how far, is every difference</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3103.47" y="-4388" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">on the way applicable in place. Answers NOOP,</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3158.47" y="-4370" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">DIFF or FULL with the reasons.</text>
</g>
<!-- variant_updater -->
<g id="node7" class="node">
<title>variant_updater</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="1182.22,-3968 826.11,-3968 826.11,-3788 1182.22,-3788 1182.22,-3968"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="846.17" y="-3937" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">VariantUpdater + VariantBulkLoader</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="850.67" y="-3909" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Create or move one variant, and load a whole</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="865.17" y="-3891" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">day into many. Everything that can refuse</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="854.17" y="-3873" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">runs before anything is created: the scenario</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="867.17" y="-3855" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">check without a query, the one multi&#45;side</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="872.17" y="-3837" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">chain query, the stored pdb:variantSafe</text>
</g>
<!-- rdf_db_connection -->
<g id="node8" class="node">
<title>rdf_db_connection</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="1171.72,-3080 836.61,-3080 836.61,-2900 1171.72,-2900 1171.72,-3080"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="926.67" y="-3040" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDbConnection</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="870.17" y="-3012" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">An open connection: owns the SPARQL</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="871.67" y="-2994" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">repository and the HTTP client, lists the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="856.67" y="-2976" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">scenarios of the database, uploads CGMES</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="920.17" y="-2958" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">files into one, clears one.</text>
</g>
<!-- rdf_db_materializer -->
<g id="node9" class="node">
<title>rdf_db_materializer</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="1899.34,-4052 1543.22,-4052 1543.22,-3872 1899.34,-3872 1899.34,-4052"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1642.28" y="-4021" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDbMaterializer</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1563.28" y="-3993" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">The slow route that always works: base graphs</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1590.78" y="-3975" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">into a local store, the differences of the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1581.78" y="-3957" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">chain folded into one and applied as plain</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1564.78" y="-3939" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">RDF, then the unchanged CGMES conversion.</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1584.78" y="-3921" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Registers the identity of the target on the</text>
</g>
<!-- version_graph -->
<g id="node10" class="node">
<title>version_graph</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="1907.34,-3390 1535.22,-3390 1535.22,-3210 1907.34,-3210 1907.34,-3390"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1596.28" y="-3359" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">VersionGraph (per scenario)</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1555.28" y="-3331" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">The planner: one query whose UNION binds both</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1557.28" y="-3313" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">ends and whose pdb:parent* walks each of them</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1564.28" y="-3295" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">to the root, then a lowest&#45;common&#45;ancestor on</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1566.78" y="-3277" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">the two chains. Answers NOOP, DIFF with the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="1567.78" y="-3259" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">path, or FULL with the reasons. A snapshot of</text>
</g>
<!-- variant_scope -->
<g id="node11" class="node">
<title>variant_scope</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="4214.6,-4211 3845.49,-4211 3845.49,-4031 4214.6,-4031 4214.6,-4211"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3971.54" y="-4180" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">VariantScope</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3883.54" y="-4152" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Makes the network be one of its variants for</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3922.54" y="-4134" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">the duration of an operation: the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3865.54" y="-4116" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">CgmesMetadataModels extension, the case date</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3884.04" y="-4098" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">and the snapshot identity of that variant are</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3883.54" y="-4080" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">swapped in, the working variant is selected,</text>
</g>
<!-- model_catalog -->
<g id="node12" class="node">
<title>model_catalog</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="4203.6,-3141.06 3856.49,-3141.06 3856.49,-2958.94 4203.6,-2958.94 4203.6,-3141.06"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3876.54" y="-3121" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">ModelCatalog (metadata graph per</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3989.04" y="-3097" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">scenario)</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3890.54" y="-3069" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Reads and writes the model nodes of one</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3878.54" y="-3051" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">scenario: which profile, which named graphs,</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3880.54" y="-3033" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">which model is superseded, how deep in the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3886.04" y="-3015" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">chain, whether every property is applicable</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="3905.54" y="-2997" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">in place. The index a client navigates</text>
</g>
<!-- graph_fetcher -->
<g id="node13" class="node">
<title>graph_fetcher</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="2627.45,-3869 2289.34,-3869 2289.34,-3689 2627.45,-3689 2627.45,-3869"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2329.39" y="-3838" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">GraphFetcher + GraphCache</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2309.39" y="-3810" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Parallel bulk transfer of the named graphs of</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2311.39" y="-3792" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">a scenario into a local in&#45;memory store: one</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2316.39" y="-3774" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">GET per graph, N&#45;Triples parsed while the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2309.89" y="-3756" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">response arrives, a single overlapped writer,</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2349.89" y="-3738" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">optional reuse of parsed graphs.</text>
</g>
<!-- rdf_db_diff_source -->
<g id="node14" class="node">
<title>rdf_db_diff_source</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="2637.45,-3579 2279.34,-3579 2279.34,-3399 2637.45,-3399 2637.45,-3579"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2299.39" y="-3539" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">RdfDbDiffSource + StatementCodec</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2309.39" y="-3511" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">Fetches the forward and reverse graphs of a</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2316.39" y="-3493" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">whole chain in one query and decodes the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2305.89" y="-3475" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">triples back into CgmesStatements, the exact</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2345.39" y="-3457" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">inverse of what the sink encoded.</text>
</g>
<!-- snapshot_catalog -->
<g id="node15" class="node">
<title>snapshot_catalog</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="2631.45,-4159 2285.34,-4159 2285.34,-3979 2631.45,-3979 2631.45,-4159"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2317.89" y="-4128" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">SnapshotCatalog (per scenario)</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2305.39" y="-4100" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">The snapshots of one scenario: putFull writes</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2316.89" y="-4082" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">the root out of instance files, putDiff a new</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2312.39" y="-4064" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">version on the head of a timestep. One root</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2323.89" y="-4046" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">per scenario, a linear version chain, and</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="2309.89" y="-4028" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">every rule enforced by the guard of the write</text>
</g>
<!-- variant_binding -->
<g id="node16" class="node">
<title>variant_binding</title>
<polygon fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="0" points="4912.21,-4596 4573.1,-4596 4573.1,-4416 4912.21,-4416 4912.21,-4596"/>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="4679.16" y="-4565" font-family="Arial" font-size="20.00" fill="#eff6ff">VariantBinding</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="4599.16" y="-4537" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">What one IIDM variant of a network stands</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="4618.16" y="-4519" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">for: the snapshot address, its IRI, the</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="4604.66" y="-4501" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">stored model per profile, the case date of</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="4593.16" y="-4483" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">that moment and which variant it was cloned</text>
<text xml:space="preserve" text-anchor="start" x="4600.16" y="-4465" font-family="Arial" font-size="15.00" fill="#bfdbfe">from. Kept on the provenance, in step with</text>
</g>
